# promise: #730
# ⌘T found only what history.json kept, the newest 5,000 pages Cra recorded itself, and Chrome deleted every
# visit older than 90 days. Arc's bar asks the profile's Chromium history, which Arc keeps whole. The fixture's
# Chromium History has two pages history.json doesn't have: one visited 10 days before the fixture was made,
# one 400 days before. Both come up in ⌘T. Chrome's expirer started 30 s after History opened and would have
# deleted the old visit, and its page with it; 40 s later ⌘T still finds it.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false, "searchSuggestions": false}
profile ${FIXTURES}/HistoryProfile
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=start
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1
wait 1
cra://commandbar?query=haystack
wait 2
cra://debug?commandBarRows=first
expect-log Cra command bar rows first: .*haystack-recent\.example\.com
expect-log Cra command bar rows first: .*haystack-ancient\.example\.com
cra://dismiss
wait 40
cra://commandbar?query=hayst
wait 2
cra://debug?commandBarRows=later
expect-log Cra command bar rows later: .*haystack-ancient\.example\.com
cra://dismiss
